## Archive 3: Library of Congress Gottscho-Schleisner Collection

### Overview

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Collection** | Gottscho-Schleisner Photograph Collection |
| **Repository** | Library of Congress Prints and Photographs Division |
| **Search URL** | `https://www.loc.gov/pictures/collection/gsc/?q=World+Trade+Center` |
| **API URL** | `https://www.loc.gov/pictures/collection/gsc/?q=World+Trade+Center&fo=json` |
| **Access** | Public domain |
| **Rights** | No known restrictions on publication |

### File Inventory

| Category | Estimated Count | Estimated Size |
|---|---|---|
| Construction photographs (1966-1973) | 50-200 photos | 250MB-1GB |
| Exterior photographs (completed) | 50-100 photos | 250MB-500MB |
| Interior photographs | 30-100 photos | 150MB-500MB |
| Plaza and site photographs | 20-50 photos | 100MB-250MB |
| **Total** | **150-450 photos** | **750MB-2.25GB** |

### Acquisition Method

**Method A — LoC API bulk download:**
```bash
# Search the collection via API
curl -sL "https://www.loc.gov/pictures/collection/gsc/?q=World+Trade+Center&fo=json&c=500" | \
  python3 -c "
import json,sys
d=json.load(sys.stdin)
for item in d.get('results',[]):
    print(item.get('image_url',''), item.get('title',''))
" > /tmp/loc_wtc_urls.txt

# Download each photo
while read url title; do
    wget -q --timeout=30 -O "WTC_CORPUS/construction-photos/$(echo $title | tr ' ' '_').jpg" "$url"
done < /tmp/loc_wtc_urls.txt
```

**Method B — Manual browser download:**
1. Visit `https://www.loc.gov/pictures/collection/gsc/?q=World+Trade+Center`
2. For each result, click the image
3. Download the highest-resolution TIFF available
4. Save to `WTC_CORPUS/construction-photos/`

**Method C — LoC bulk download tool:**
```bash
# The Library of Congress supports bulk downloads via their API
# Each item has a direct image URL accessible via the JSON API
curl -sL "https://www.loc.gov/pictures/collection/gsc/?q=World+Trade+Center&fo=json" | \
  python3 -c "import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d.get('pagination',{}).get('of','?'), 'total results')"
```

